"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Preoperative PSA was 4.6. The surgical findings included a Gleason 4+3 (ISUP grade group 3) and pathological stage pT2c, with positive surgical margins and no seminal vesicle invasion. The absence of lymph nodes removed is noted, and lymphovascular invasion was absent. The biopsy showed a Gleason 3+3 (ISUP grade group 1). The lack of documented nodal sampling widens uncertainty regarding true nodal status, as pNx is not equivalent to pN0.\n\nThe primary driver for prognosis is the pathological stage and margin status. Countervailing factors include the lower biopsy grade compared to the resection and the absence of lymphovascular invasion. Information that would revise this prognosis significantly includes postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory. The current uncertainty regarding nodal status due to missing sampling is a key limitation. The fixed estimated horizon is 62.79 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 37.67–87.91 months; its coverage has not been validated."
